WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.350
An audit goes in. A cited risk score and a
human-approved action plan come out.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.235
Reviewing a supplier audit takes hours,

00:00:10.235 --> 00:00:14.525
and an AI summary that invents findings is
worse than none.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:20.104
The Supply Chain Compliance Co-Pilot is a
multi-agent system:

00:00:20.104 --> 00:00:23.575
a supervisor routing five specialist
workers.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:29.815
The workflow is compliance-grade. The
model only structures and phrases;

00:00:29.815 --> 00:00:33.350
code scores, verifies and gates every
decision.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.901
A supervisor assembles the team,

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:41.825
and the analyst works the four SMETA-style
pillars in parallel.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:48.743
Each non-conformance carries a verbatim
quote, checked against the uploaded audit.

00:00:48.743 --> 00:00:51.950
Fabricated citations are dropped and
counted.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.025
Corrective actions pause for a human
decision,

00:00:56.025 --> 00:00:59.150
then are sealed in a hash-chained audit
trail.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.884
Every prompt is versioned in a registry.

00:01:03.884 --> 00:01:07.241
Promotion is gated by evaluation and
audited,

00:01:07.241 --> 00:01:10.300
and each run records its prompt versions.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:15.895
In the evaluation gate, fabricated quotes
measure zero,

00:01:15.895 --> 00:01:19.600
against about ten percent for a single
bare prompt.

